        answer: "An improvement exchange uses the exchange accommodation titleholder safe harbor from Revenue Procedure 2000-37, where the exchange accommodation titleholder holds title to the replacement property while exchange proceeds, released through the qualified intermediary, fund construction draws for improvements. Once the one hundred eighty-day deadline approaches, title transfers to the taxpayer, and the improvements completed by that point are counted as part of the exchange value.",
