        question: "What counts as a related party in an Oklahoma City, OK 1031 exchange?",
        answer: "A related party generally includes family members such as siblings, spouses, ancestors, and lineal descendants, along with entities in which the taxpayer owns more than fifty percent, and other relationships defined by cross-reference to related-party provisions elsewhere in the tax code. For an Oklahoma City, OK investor, this most commonly comes up when exchanging property with a sibling, an adult child, or a commonly controlled family entity.",
