        question: "How much gain can be excluded on a home sale in Oklahoma City, OK?",
        answer: "A single taxpayer can generally exclude up to two hundred fifty thousand dollars of gain, and a married couple filing jointly can generally exclude up to five hundred thousand dollars of gain, on the sale of a home owned and used as a primary residence for at least two of the five years before the sale, under Section 121 of the Internal Revenue Code.",
